  "modules": [
    {
      "id": "uniequip_001_clour",
      "name": {
        "en": "Vermeil's Badge",
        "zh": "红云证章",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "INITIAL",
      "typeName2": "",
      "icon": "original",
      "description": {
        "en": "Operator Vermeil has demonstrated a remarkable aptitude for maintaining distance whilst conducting suppressive fire against the enemy.\nThe Field Operations Department has thus passed the following resolution:\nThis operator shall be appointed a Sniper Operator during field operations to exercise Marksman responsibilities.\nIn witness whereof,\nThis badge is hereby conferred upon the above named.",
        "zh": "干员红云擅长保持距离对敌人进行火力压制\n根据外勤部门决议\n在外勤任务中划分为狙击干员，行使速射手职责\n特别颁发此证章\n以兹证明",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "uniequip_002_clour",
      "name": {
        "en": "'Still Alive'",
        "zh": "“不落”",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "ADVANCED",
      "typeName2": "X",
      "icon": "uniequip_002_clour",
      "description": {
        "en": "In the barrens stands a newly planted flag. No one knows who put it there, nor what settlement it belongs to. It's lifted by a crude pole stuck into the earth, wind sweeping up sand and flying the banner straight.\nA passerby sees the design upon it and is struck by vague familiarity, but where he's seen it before totally escapes him. A cloth with the same design covers the grain pile back at his home, dust having long worn that special symbol away.\nHe sees the towering flag and pulls out his hatchet, thinking to cut the flagpole down. The fabric seems sturdy and strong, the pole suitable for firewood. Unwanted by anyone, he may as well chop it down and put it to better use. Just like how every settlement in this stretch of the wild fights one another over soil and resources, ultimately evolving into ever more brand-new civilizations.\nThe axe hacks into the pole, but cannot cut it. He puts a hand out to shake it, but the flag defiantly flies even straighter in greeting the sun. He hocks a glob of spit onto the ground, shifts away from the light, and squints his eyes as he looks up. The material's very new. Not yet stained by rain or dirt. The burlap flaunts its sheen.\nA few days ago, a mechanical arm brushed aside the traps set all around its cabin home, picking flax from the long-forsaken waste, and weaving as its Mom and Dad once taught it. The hand so used to bows was somewhat clumsy, but the metal hand briskly rolled the flax into thread.\nSuppose one said this arm used to be treasured for how it could draw a bow with greater force—now, it had its owner's full interest for how meticulously it could weave. But the mechanical arm understood none of this; it simply followed its master's will, making good on what she saw fit.\nA few years ago, the arm's owner thankfully told the old man that installed it how she would use it to further her revenge. In time, she used the greater force within it to loose arrows into the bodies of mercenaries. She looked at the things they left behind, at the unfamiliar symbol on them—the story of her. Time stopped here, and not a soul remembers all that he was before. She pulled her cloak off, fixing it tight to the wound that almost saw her windpipe slit open. Revenge can easily wipe away a person's past. She didn't want to turn out the same way when her demise came.\nSo she returned to her home, wove this mantle, sought out a firm flagpole, and stuck it rigidly into the soil.\nIt is the final remaining symbol of this settlement in the wilds, and she used her vengeful arm to weave this memento of civilization. The flag rises, the steel arm's owner walks her new path, and those who pass by the banner will recall the pattern she wove.",
        "zh": "荒野上新树立起一面旗帜，没人知道这是谁立起来的，又是属于哪个聚落的。它被一根粗糙的旗杆支起，扎在土地上，风席卷着沙砾，把它扯得紧绷。\n一个路过的人看着旗帜上的花纹，隐隐觉得眼熟，却完全想不起自己是在哪里见过。在他的家中，有着同样花纹的布匹盖在谷堆上，尘土早就模糊了那个特殊的符号。\n他看着这面突兀的旗帜，掏出斧子想要砍断旗杆。旗帜的布料看起来结实耐用，旗杆也能用来烧火取暖。既然是没人要的东西，不如砍下来发挥更好的作用。就像是这片荒野上的各个聚落，因为土地和资源互相争夺与吞并，最终会演化成更多全新的文明。\n斧子凿在旗杆上，却没能砍断，他又伸手去摇，旗帜反而随着风更加笔直地迎接阳光。他往地上啐了一口唾沫，避开太阳眯着眼睛往上看，料子很新，还没沾上雨水和尘土，粗麻闪着光泽。\n几天前，一只机械的手臂拨开家乡小屋四周的陷阱，采摘了早已无人看管荒废的粗麻，按照父母当初教授的方法细细编制。拿惯了弓的手有些笨拙，机械手却灵活地揉搓起麻绳。\n如果说这只手臂曾经因为能更有力地拉开弓弦而受到喜爱，它现在则是因为能更精细地编织而备受主人的关注。但机械的手臂不懂这些，它只是跟随着主人的意愿，去完成她的想法。\n几年前，手臂的主人对着为她安上胳膊的老人感激地说自己会用它来更好地复仇，后来，她用这只更加充满力量的手臂把箭射入那些佣兵的身体。她看着佣兵留下的东西，和上面陌生的符号——这个人的故事。时间停在这里，没人记得他之前的一切。她扯下自己身上的披风，紧紧地按在差点割到她喉管的伤口上。复仇能轻易地抹掉一个人的过往，她不希望自己的聚落也变成这样。\n所以她返回了自己的家乡，编织起这顶披风，寻来坚固的旗杆，把它死死地钉进了土地。\n它是这个聚落留在荒野上的最后一个象征，她用复仇的胳膊编下文明的纪念。旗帜在飞扬，钢铁手臂的主人走上了新的道路，路过旗帜的人们会记住她编织出的纹样。",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
